+## `net`
+
+Access: capability `net`.
+
+Capability `net` (experimental): a connection-scoped channel between the client and server components with the SAME mod id. Never an internet socket.
+
+### record `session`
+
+Opaque host-generated connection token, not a player identity or permission.
+
+| Field | Type | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `high` | `u64` |  |
+| `low` | `u64` |  |
+
+### record `message`
+
+| Field | Type | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `player` | `option<string>` | On the server, the authenticated sender's UUID. On the client, none. |
+| `session` | `option<session>` | Server only: host token captured at enqueue time. Compare with session-token if retaining a message across ticks/reconnections. |
+| `data` | `list<u8>` |  |
+
+### variant `event`
+
+| Case | Payload | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `received` | `message` |  |
+| `disconnected` |  | Client connection ended or changed. Discard old session/prediction. |
+
+| Function | Signature | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `connected` | `func() -> bool` | Client: the server announced channel support. Server: false (use the online players instead). No channel is available on a vanilla server. |
+| `session-token` | `func(player: string) -> option<session>` | Server only: fresh token for this player's current authenticated connection, available after its first received message. None elsewhere. |
+| `send` | `func(player: option<string>, data: list<u8>) -> result<_, string>` | Client: player must be none, sends to its server. Server: player must name an online player's UUID. Host supplies the sending mod id and authenticates players; bytes never select their sender. At most 16 KiB per message and 8 messages per hook. An error queues nothing. |
+| `poll` | `func() -> list<event>` | Events in arrival order. Bounded to 64 events / 256 KiB; no polling does not grant unbounded memory. Disconnect clears old queued messages. |
